{title: Come, Thou Almighty King}
{artist: Anonymous, in Collection of Hymns for Social Worship}
{key: G}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 3/4}
{meta: tune ITALIAN HYMN - Felice de Giardini (1769)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1757, tune 1769: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Come, Thou Al[D]mighty [G]King, help us Thy [D]name to sing,
[G]Help us to [C]praise! [G]Father, all [D]glorious,
[G]O'er all vic[D]torious, [G]come, and reign [C]over us,
[G]Ancient of [D]Days[G]!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Come, Thou In[D]carnate [G]Word, gird on Thy [D]mighty sword,
[G]Our prayer at[C]tend! [G]Come, and Thy [D]people bless,
[G]And give Thy [D]word success; [G]Spirit of [C]holiness,
[G]On us de[D]scend[G]!
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]To Thee, great [D]One in [G]Three, eternal [D]praises be,
[G]Hence ever[C]more. [G]Thy sovereign [D]majesty
[G]May we in [D]glory see, [G]and to e[C]ternity
[G]Love and a[D]dore[G]!
{end_of_verse}
